<title>UK: RUSSIA'S NOVOROSSIISK OIL PORT REOPENS AFTER STORM.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA'S NOVOROSSIISK OIL PORT REOPENS AFTER STORM.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea reopened on Monday after closing for 10 hours due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port shut for three hours on Sunday afternoon because of a thunderstorm, reopening at 1900 local only for high winds and swell to close it again at 2250.</p>
<p>Operations resumed at 0615 local on Monday when the weather improved. Two crude oil tankers were alongside and another two were waiting at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>Other oil ports on the Black Sea and Baltic were open and working normally, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
